 "intro": {
  "text": "The London System is a calm way to start a game as White, with a clear plan for your first moves. The bishop from c1 comes out to f4 early, before your e-pawn moves and blocks its path. Then pawns on d4, e3 and c3 make a solid wall in the centre, and your knights come out to f3 and d2. In this Lesson Black answers in a solid way, and you build the whole set-up."
 },
